  "questions": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "id": "2441876595719898299_77767",
      "question": "For the point, name this president of Gran Colombia, known to some as \"The Liberator.\n\"",
      "meta": {
        "category": "Latin America",
        "era": "05",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "id": "nonteam_more_057",
      "question": "It also recognized Cuban independence.\nFor the point, name this 1898 treaty signed in the French capital.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "World",
        "era": "05",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "id": "team_more_043",
      "question": "It lost the presidency in 2000 when Vicente Fox won for the PAN.\nFor the point, name this party often abbreviated PRI.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "Latin America",
        "era": "07",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "id": "team_more_069",
      "question": "It prompted stricter laws against enslaved people and free Black communities in the American South.\nFor the point, name this uprising led by a man with the first name Nat.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "North America",
        "era": "05",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "id": "team_more_100",
      "question": "It created India and Pakistan while princely states chose which country to join.\nFor the point, name this division of the subcontinent.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "South Asia",
        "era": "06",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "id": "team_more_035",
      "question": "He won at Cannae but could not capture Rome before being defeated years later at Zama.\nFor the point, name this Carthaginian general.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "Africa",
        "era": "02",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "id": "7189817323075011549_77766",
      "question": "This man described the uncertainty of ongoing battles as the \"Fog of War,\" and he said, \"War was the Continuation of Politics by another means.\n\" For the point, name this 19th century German military theorist who wrote On War.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "Europe",
        "era": "05",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "id": "nonteam_more_068",
      "question": "It was founded by Chandragupta with advice from Chanakya.\nFor the point, name this ancient Indian empire.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "South Asia",
        "era": "02",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "id": "team_more_011",
      "question": "It escalated after taxes such as the Stamp Act and Tea Act, then produced a declaration adopted in Philadelphia in 1776.\nFor the point, name this struggle that created the United States.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "North America",
        "era": "05",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "id": "team_more_014",
      "question": "It defeated a British force at Isandlwana before losing later in 1879.\nFor the point, name this southern African kingdom.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "Africa",
        "era": "05",
        "source": "original"
      }
    }
  ]
